course: dictionary
lesson: 11156
title: Wimp and wimping out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wimp is a person who seems weak, scared or not brave. It is an informal word, so you will hear it in playgrounds and stories more than in formal writing. «Sam won't climb the fence into the building site, so Jake calls him a wimp.» Sam is not climbing because he is scared, and Jake uses wimp to say he is not brave.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Sam won't climb, and Jake calls him a wimp. The reason is the clue: Sam is holding back because he is scared. So a wimp is someone who seems scared to try something. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «Sam won't climb the fence, so Jake calls him a person who seems scared.» It still makes sense.
explain: Wimp can also be a verb. To wimp out means to decide not to do something because you feel scared. For example, «I was going to try the zip wire, but I wimped out at the top.» Wimp out is informal, so keep it for chatting, not for formal writing.
explain: Be careful with this word. Calling someone a wimp is unkind, and it can be teasing or bullying. Everyone feels scared sometimes, so choose words that help people, not words that hurt them.
fact: A wimp is a person who seems weak, scared or not brave.
fact: To wimp out means to decide not to do something because you are scared.
fact: Wimp is informal, and calling someone a wimp can be unkind, teasing or bullying.
fact: Phrases you may hear are: don't be a wimp, wimp out of, and a bit of a wimp.
fact: The adjective wimpy describes someone or something that acts weak or scared, and it is also informal.
exercise: «Sam won't climb the fence into the building site, so Jake calls him a wimp.» What does wimp mean here? | A person who builds houses | A person who is very strong | *A person who seems scared or not brave | A person who likes climbing fences
exercise: Ella says, «I was going to try the zip wire, but I wimped out.» What does wimped out mean? | Lost her way home | Ran all the way to the top | Did it very fast and well | *Decided not to do it because she was scared
exercise: Your friend is scared of the high diving board. Which is the kind thing to say? | Everyone is watching, so hurry up. | Don't be such a wimp. | *Take your time, we can try again together later. | Only wimps wear armbands.
test: Why is calling someone a wimp unkind? | It means they are kind | It is always the right word for a scared friend | It shows they are the best at everything | *It can hurt their feelings and turn into teasing or bullying
test: Jayden says, «Mia wimped out of the spelling bee.» What does that mean? | Mia won the spelling bee | *Mia decided not to take part because she felt scared | Mia forgot how to spell | Mia wrote the spelling very quickly
exam: Which word is the adjective that describes someone acting like a wimp? | wimp out | *wimpy | wimping out | wimps
